in @prism
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/lens

# @mirror/lens/refract — the grammar-graph spectrum lens.
#
# The measurement glass at the grammar-graph altitude. Reads the five
# Void dualities (entropy / spectral / cheeger / ricci / mixing) over
# the grammar graph and surfaces them as verdicts; the gutter rendering
# layer's input.
#
# Per docs/specs/trace-kintsugi-pipeline.md: "@mirror/refract IS bench
# wearing its real name." The substrate has been measuring itself
# spectrally at the grammar-graph altitude for over a month; the lens
# family naming closes the recognition. Per
# docs/insights/2026-06-06-benchmarking-glass-sweep.md §2.2: refract
# observes the SHAPE of the grammar; transit observes the COST of
# executing it. Two layers of the same observation tower.
#
# === Why refract stays a namespace name ===
#
# The 2026-06-04 operation-altitude rename (refract → settle) was at
# the algebra altitude: every Prism has a `settle` operation, not a
# `refract` operation. The optical-dispersion metaphor lifted to the
# family altitude where it stays load-bearing: a measurement lens IS
# refraction — the grammar graph enters, the five dualities disperse
# the structure into bands, the verdicts come out. The namespace
# `@mirror/lens/refract` carries the family-altitude metaphor without
# competing for the operation name.
#
# === Five Void dualities (per trace-kintsugi-pipeline.md §1.1) ===
#
#   entropy   Von Neumann entropy of the normalized graph Laplacian.
#             Order ↔ disorder. Low = rigid/crystallized. High = chaotic.
#   spectral  Fiedler value (λ_2 of graph Laplacian). Connectivity ↔
#             fragility. High = robust mesh. Low = fragile.
#   cheeger   Cheeger constant (minimum edge boundary ratio). Flow ↔
#             bottleneck. High = smooth data flow. Low = SPOF.
#   ricci     Forman-Ricci curvature per edge. Geometric pressure on
#             individual edges.
#   mixing    random-walk mixing time. How fast information equilibrates
#             across the graph.
#
# Each duality is a property; each verdict is the glass-floor
# verdict; the joint report is transparency<duality>. Same monoid as
# @mirror/lens/transit; same eigenboard-tagged envelope.
#
# === Family placement ===
#
# Sixth species under @mirror/lens. Measurement-shape lens at the
# grammar-graph altitude (sibling to lens/transit at the body altitude).
# Per the benchmarking-glass-sweep §2.2: "refract observes the SHAPE of
# the grammar; transit observes the COST of executing it."
#
# === Body status ===
#
# FAMILY-HEADER ONLY this tick. The five-duality property type is
# declared as a closed sum; the measurement surface (the bench infrastructure
# already living in mirror, per trace-kintsugi-pipeline.md) lands via
# obligation blocks; bodies (Fiedler-vector computation, von Neumann
# entropy, Forman-Ricci, mixing time) live in the bootstrap's spectral
# layer (bootstrap/src/spectral.rs) and lift into mirror as the
# substrate-pull discipline matures.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/trace-kintsugi-pipeline.md (the bench-as-
#               refract recognition),
#               docs/insights/2026-06-06-benchmarking-glass-sweep.md
#               §2.2 (refract as measurement-at-grammar-graph altitude),
#               docs/specs/the-convergence.md (the four-transport
#               family this measurement lens sits beside).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]]
#                      (the dualities ARE linear-algebraic properties
#                      of the graph Laplacian).
# Related shards: lens.mirror (family root),
#                 lens/transit.mirror (sibling measurement lens at the
#                 body altitude),
#                 glass.mirror (verdict + transparency).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/lens/refract.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/lens/refract` and only that.

# === duality family — the five Void dualities ===
#
# Closed sum. Each variant names one spectral measurement of the
# grammar graph; downstream consumers (the gutter rendering layer)
# match on the variant to pick a color.
type duality = entropy | spectral | cheeger | ricci | mixing

# === refract report — transparency<duality> ===
#
# Per trace-kintsugi-pipeline.md: refract's output is the five-duality
# spectrum of the grammar graph at one snapshot. transparency(duality)
# is the glass-floor loss carrier parametric on the duality axis;
# verdicts compose under the same monoid lens/transit uses (one algebra,
# many consumers).
type report = {
  verdicts: transparency(duality),
}

# === measurement surface — abstract; bodies on consumer pull ===

# measure — read a grammar graph and produce a refract report. The
# bodies (Fiedler-vector, von-Neumann-entropy, Forman-Ricci, Cheeger,
# random-walk mixing) live in bootstrap/src/spectral.rs today; lift
# into substrate as substrate-pull matures.
measure(graph: ref, d: [duality]) -> report { \ }

# stabilize — the kintsugi-pipeline halting condition. Loss stabilizes
# when eⁿ⁺¹ ≥ eⁿ (per trace-kintsugi-pipeline.md §0). The substrate
# reads this as the crystal-formation signal.
stabilize(prev: report, next: report) -> verdict { \ }

out @mirror/lens/refract
out duality
out report
out measure
out stabilize
